# Docs taxonomy

Platform markdown is centralized. New `.md` files must follow the path policy enforced by `pnpm check:docs-layout` (`scripts/check-docs-layout.ts`), which runs in `validate:ci`.

## Allowed locations

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `docs/guides/*.md` | Cross-cutting behavior guides (kebab-case, **no** `-guide` suffix) |
| `docs/reference/*.md` | JSON contract SSOTs (entity, metric, query, data-hook, custom-view) |
| `docs/ai-platform/**/*.md` | AI stack architecture and integration |
| `docs/infrastructure/**/*.md` | GCP, CI/CD, WIF, workloads |
| `docs/ui-design-manual/**/*.md` | Layout JSON handoff / recipes / SYNC |
| `docs/README.md` | Index |
| Root `README.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Monorepo overview / agent workload policy |
| `.github/**/*.md` | GitHub docs |
| `apps/**/README.md`, `packages/**/README.md`, `scripts/**/README.md` | Local package/app contracts only |

Anywhere else: **only** `README.md` under apps/packages/scripts — not free-form guides.

## Naming

- Guides: `firestore-collections.md`, not `firestore-collections-guide.md`
- Reference: contract name + `-definition.md` where applicable
- Prefer linking from `docs/README.md` when adding a top-level guide/reference

## Choosing a folder

| If the doc is… | Put it in… |
|----------------|------------|
| How a subsystem works across apps | `docs/guides/` |
| Import/export JSON shape for catalogs | `docs/reference/` |
| AI controller, spend, RAG, chat | `docs/ai-platform/` |
| Deploy, secrets, Terraform, workloads | `docs/infrastructure/` |
| Layout/component JSON for designers/AI | `docs/ui-design-manual/` |
| Package-local API surface | that package’s `README.md` |

## Exceptions

One-off paths must be added to `EXTRA_ALLOWLIST` in `scripts/check-docs-layout.ts` (rare). Do not invent new top-level doc folders without updating the checker and `docs/README.md`.

## Do not

- Leave planning / handoff markdown at repo root (except `README.md` / `AGENTS.md`)
- Duplicate long guides inside packages (link to `docs/` instead)
- Put tenant-specific docs in `docs/` — tenant notes stay under `.local/`

## Enforcement

- `pnpm check:docs-layout`
- `pnpm validate:ci` / `pnpm validate:local`

## References

- Index: `docs/README.md`
- Checker: `scripts/check-docs-layout.ts`
